  "notes": "1h serial soak plus on-device TF/KEY assist windows on the final hardened firmware (tree of d73cadb; dirty=tools/tests collector additions only, poc/ untouched). VERDICT FAIL: single failing criterion - console 'wifi reconnect' never returns to CONNECTED (0/5 cycles in soak + 0/1 controlled reproduction). Root cause: wifi_service.cc reconnect() calls esp_wifi_connect() while still associated; IDF v6 rejects it ('sta is connected, disconnect before connecting to new ap'), no STA_DISCONNECTED event fires, so the event-driven auto-reconnect never engages; app state stays CONNECTING indefinitely. connect_stored() path (boot auto-connect, portal) is unaffected because it disconnects first. Follow-up fix task required. All other soak criteria PASS: 358 JSONL lines (360 +/-10), sequence 25..384 strictly monotonic, zero status:FAILED lines, reset_reason=11 constant across all samples, uptime monotonic (no reboot), tf=READY throughout, no spurious key presses. internal_free memory-decline criterion: N/A - firmware exposes no heap field in either JSON stream (telemetry or status --json); not instrumented, follow-up candidate. Assist windows: W1 KEY >=3s portal hold PASS (AP up observed, auto-recovery to CONNECTED within 120s without console help); W1 short/long presses completed via W2 retry: exactly +2/+2, no spurious; W2 TF: 2 pull->insert cycles, 4/4 transitions ABSENT+tf_logging false / READY+resume, logging_error=0; W3 absent-boot: TF-absent classified <=0.9s device time (W(835) frame-sd probe failed), health DEGRADED never FAILED, alive >30s, no telemetry while card out, reinsert resumed logging. TF same-file append judged behaviorally: sequence continuity across W2 pull/reinsert cycles and resumed logging across the W3 reboot with logging_error=0; direct TF line counts are not observable over UART (no fs listing command). Watch items: rtc_valid=false in all soak status samples after a transient PCF85063 ESP_ERR_INVALID_CRC during an earlier USB glitch (was true at session start); boot-moment telemetry status:FAILED artifact (T10-known) absent here because the capture attached mid-boot. Deviation: status responses artifact committed as status.ndjson (frame-evidence discovers every *.json under poc/evidence and NDJSON is not a manifest); soak raw directory kept outside poc/evidence because the collector's status.json artifact would be discovered by frame-evidence as an invalid manifest; curated copies are committed here instead. raw-history/ archives all /tmp/opencode/m1-verify serial captures from T4-T11 and this task."
